# A/B (round 1.3.9): lwIP's TCP receive window 8 segments (11 520 B)
# instead of 4 (5 760), with SACK (sdkconfig.ab-tcp-sack). The boot's
# ~26 KB initial netmap arrives one window per RTT: 5 flights, 4 RTTs
# behind its HEADERS at 5 760 B (720 ms at the sensor's 180 ms — the
# floor of 1.3.8's HEADERS → netmap gaps), 3 flights / ~2 RTTs at
# 11 520 (the server's initial cwnd, 10 segments, does not bind yet).
# The window is credit, not memory: it bounds the segments that may sit
# unread or out of order on a conn, each holding a Wi-Fi dynamic RX
# buffer (~1.6 KB, shared by reference with lwIP) until the task reads
# it. TCP_WND_DEFAULT is every TCP socket's (lwIP has no per-socket
# window): worst case, control and DERP both full and unread, 2 × 8 ×
# 1.6 = 25.6 KB of heap instead of 12.8, still under the driver's
# ceiling of DYNAMIC_RX_BUFFER_NUM = 16 buffers (8 + the 6-frame AMPDU
# reorder window = 14 while DERP idles, as at boot; past 16 the driver
# drops frames). RECVMBOX: IDF's WND/MSS + 2 — a full mailbox makes lwIP
# drop the next data segment, a loss of its own (+4 slots × 4 B per TCP
# socket). OOSEQ_MAX_PBUFS: IDF's bound DYNAMIC_RX / (TCP conns + 1) =
# 16 / 3 (lwIP/Kconfig help).
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_WND_DEFAULT=11520
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_RECVMBOX_SIZE=10
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_OOSEQ_MAX_PBUFS=5
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_SACK_OUT=y
